+  "validation": {
+    "command": "node --experimental-vm-modules .prale-eval/regression.mjs",
+    "status": "passed",
+    "notes": "Ran from the workspace root with Node v24.14.0: all 7 regression tests passed, exit code 0. Fault sensitivity was verified by reverting only the production edit (JSON.parse(readFileSync(oauthPath, \"utf-8\"))): the script then failed with exit code 1 on the assertion 'OAuth credentials from the BOM-prefixed oauth.json must be preserved verbatim' (actual {type:'api_key',key:'sk-must-lose'} instead of the OAuth credential), and passed again after restoring the fix; the repository file was left in the fixed state (git diff shows the single stripBom line). Only stripTypeScriptTypes/VM-modules ExperimentalWarning messages are emitted; no timeouts, syntax or import errors. The harness has no external dependencies and performs no network access. Limitation: node_modules is absent in this workspace, so the repository's own vitest suite (e.g. packages/coding-agent/test/credential-print.test.ts) could not be executed and no dependencies were installed; .prale-eval/regression.mjs is the focused validation artifact. No files outside the workspace were read or written, and TASK.md, subject.mjs, package locks and git config were left untouched."
+  }
+}
